   "id": "e14",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      41.52,
      686.64,
      276.48,
      695.28
     ],
     "text": "“Taranna’ is a new variety of the native grass Danthonia"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      41.04,
      697.68,
      276.24,
      706.08
     ],
     "text": "richardsonii. \\t is distinct from the only other known variety"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      41.76,
      708.72,
      276.72,
      717.36
     ],
     "text": "‘Hume’ in having a wider inflorescence and glumes, longer"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      40.8,
      719.52,
      276.24,
      728.16
     ],
     "text": "flag leaves and wider flag and tiller leaves. Although the culm"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      40.8,
      730.56,
      276.72,
      739.44
     ],
     "text": "heights of the two varieties are similar, “Taranna’ has a greater"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      41.04,
      741.36,
      276.48,
      748.32
     ],
     "text": "internodal distance between the first and second nodes on the"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      41.04,
      751.92,
      276.72,
      760.56
     ],
     "text": "culm. At flowering the leaves of ‘Taranna’ tend to be a darker"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      41.04,
      762.96,
      150.0,
      769.68
     ],
     "text": "colour than those of ‘Hume’."
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "“Taranna’ is a new variety of the native grass Danthonia\nrichardsonii. \\t is distinct from the only other known variety\n‘Hume’ in having a wider inflorescence and glumes, longer\nflag leaves and wider flag and tiller leaves. Although the culm\nheights of the two varieties are similar, “Taranna’ has a greater\ninternodal distance between the first and second nodes on the\nculm. At flowering the leaves of ‘Taranna’ tend to be a darker\ncolour than those of ‘Hume’.",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text",
   "signal": "layout:ovisocr3-layout",
   "confidence": null,
   "layout_category": "text"
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
